 host-load runaway
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After ~24h of healthy training (step 47k → 79433), the shared host's
load avg climbed past 700 around 2026-05-25 14:30 — another job
started hammering CPU/disk/PCIe — and NCCL collectives started
stalling for tens of minutes, eventually tripping the default 10-min
timeout: '[F525 ProcessGroupNCCL.cpp:1554] Terminating the process
... due to collective timeout or exception'. Bumped the timeout to
1h, relaunch went straight to D-state on I/O without producing
output, so I parked the run at ckpt 78000 and started hourly /proc/loadavg
checks.

Load has climbed monotonically every hour for 24h since (1135 → 6081
as of 15:51), with no plateau. Adding the timeline so a future
session can see the pattern and decide whether to wait or move the
job to another node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
